        {
          "chunk_id": "chunk:ch15_genes_and_proteins:84",
          "text": "and recognizes one or more of the mRNA codons that define the order of amino acids in\na protein.\n\nAminoacyl-tRNAs bind to the ribosome and add the corresponding amino acid to the polypeptide chain. Therefore, tRNAs are the molecules that actually \u201ctranslate\u201d the language of RNA into the language of proteins. Of the 64 possible mRNA codons\u2014or triplet combinations of A, U, G, and C\u2014three specify the termination of protein\n15.5 \u2022 Ribosomes and Protein Synthesis\n407",
